# The roles a machine can play, each a set of capabilities, all of which
# must hold: ./install.sh roles says which hold here, and why. A profile's
# PROFILE-roles line in a PLUGIN file names roles from this list.
#
# The capabilities ./install.sh detects, each with its evidence:
#   xymon_server  etc/xymonserver.cfg and bin/xymond under XYMONHOME
#   xymon_client  etc/xymonclient.cfg and bin/xymonclient.sh under XYMONHOME
#   own_account   no XYMONHOME in the environment: a person's own shell
#   xymon_user    the server's xymonlaunch runs as you, or its tree is yours
# and those the probes of CAPABILITIES, beside this file, can see: ai_cli,
# an AI CLI on PATH; llm, a model answering. One that leaves no mark is
# declared: ./install.sh capability NAME.
server: xymon_server
client: xymon_client
tools: own_account
ai_workstation: own_account ai_cli
ai_server: xymon_server ai_cli llm
